{
	title: 'Commits without a Session trailer belong to the call that ran git commit',
	spec: 'Only Hal commits carry Session trailers; other projects commit without them. A commit with no trailer naming a session of this home belongs to the session whose Bash call made it, when that call command runs git ... commit (no ; & | between) and either its output prints the commit short hash or no other Bash call in the same repository with such a command was running at the commit time. In that last case the other call claims the commit when it finishes. That session gets the commit card, the commit hook (task sg0) and a notice attributed to its tab; no trailer cross-check runs. Other trailerless commits still name no session. Invariants restored: every commit an agent makes with git commit in any repository shows as a commit card in its transcript and in /find commits; a commit another session made during a call never shows under that call.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'The commit-hook integration test covers untrailed commits as owned by the Bash caller. Reset its seen-hash cache between fixture repositories: identical commit bytes created in the same second otherwise hid stale expectations through cross-test deduplication.',
		'Bug seen 2026-10-29: in ghost, tab 3 committed during another tab git commit call; that call finished first and took the commit (reflog lines carry no process). commits.state.active holds running watches; the observation release() drops them, since an unlaunched call never reaches finish. A rival must have started before the commit second ends, so a quiet commit is not lost to a call that began later. Two quiet trailerless commits racing still go to whichever finishes first.'
	],
	needs: ['pdw'],
	foldInto: ['hy']
}
